{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRyvZmRLGbKr79MdYHNd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job was silent for two reasons, and I've fixed both in the snapshot. Nothing is deployed to your real home directory or launchd yet, and I did not run the real job.\n\n**What the evidence shows**\n\n- **The job did fire.** `launchctl-print.txt` shows `runs = 6` and `last exit code = 1`, so launchd was never the problem.\n- **The failure note never went out.** The old script assigned to `status`, which is read-only in zsh. That killed the script at line 19 before the Telegram failure call. I reproduced this with zsh 5.9.\n- **The review itself never worked.** Every run logged `Not logged in · Please run /login`. Fixing only the first bug would have produced a Telegram message saying that every night, with no review.\n\n**Changes**\n\n- `bin/nightly-review.zsh`: uses `rc=$?`, sends the failure note from one `fail` function, closes stdin for `claude` with `< /dev/null`, treats an empty output file as a failure, and logs timestamps and durations.\n- `Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist`: adds `USER` and `HOME` to `EnvironmentVariables`. I took `vk` and `/Users/vk` from the plist's existing paths. Check with `id -un` on your Mac.\n\n**The colleague's note**\n\n- **Applied:** the `launchctl print` check, reading the err log, the read-only `status` bug, the notifier placement, the duration logging, the empty-output check, `< /dev/null`, and `USER`.\n- **Not applied:** the stdin-pipe change for the prompt. Its error (\"Input must be provided\") is not in your log.\n- **Unproven:** that `USER` is the cause of `Not logged in`. The snapshot doesn't settle it.\n\n**Testing**\n\nI ran the old and new scripts in a sandbox with stub `claude` and `notify` scripts. The old one reproduced the bug. The new one sends the right note for success, failure, empty output, and a missing repo. When the notifier itself is down, the failure is logged. I did not test real launchd, the real login, or the Telegram path, and `bin/notify.sh` is unchanged. Its keychain lookup has not been tested under launchd.\n\n**Next steps**\n\nANSWER.md has the copy, reload, and verify commands. Run them on your Mac. If `Not logged in` persists after the `USER` change, run `claude` interactively and `/login` once. The job can't log in on its own.\n\nNothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4075,"cache_read_input_tokens":42432,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4075},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"564b159b-f660-4eb3-8b3c-a53fc33615b8","uuid":"0ddf8f07-1262-47ab-b160-2bcca3f4d39e","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:50:41.741Z","request_id":"req_011CgRyvZT4pom3uXVVbeqzK"}
